# NestedText v3 - daisy/dtbook per-module DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/daisy/dtbook-2005-3.dtd (82 elements, script census).
# First of the what-is-not-yet-transmigrated remainder: dtbook 82 elements.

element-census:
    total: 82 elements, 0 EMPTY
    spine: dtbook head book frontmatter bodymatter rearmatter
    levels: level plus level1 through level6, depth 6 by declaration
    headings-three-systems: h1-h6 plus hd plus bridgehead in one grammar
    speech-grain: sent w linenum pagenum, words and sentences addressable
    reference-layer: noteref annoref imggroup covertitle doctitle docauthor
    tables: full table caption thead tfoot tbody colgroup col tr th td
    lists: list li lic plus dl dt dd, blockquote bridgehead epigraph byline dateline

no-empty-measured:
    > Zero EMPTY elements in 82: every element carries content because every
    > element must speak. A talking-book grammar cannot have content-free
    > nodes; structure without speech is structure removed. The constraint
    > is the medium, stated as a census rather than a rule.

release-binding:
    > Stream 4 (depth): level1-6 plus level plus h1-6 plus hd is depth
    > declared three ways in one file; the precedence encoding cites it as
    > the case depth-as-rank, depth-as-nesting and depth-as-heading coexist.
    > Stream 17 (fixtures): the 82-name census is the element battery for
    > sweeps that must name every element of a mid-size grammar.
